  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Strengthening Civil Protection and Legal Accountability to Counter Settler Violence in the West Bank</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 18-month measure seeks to enhance civilian protection, emergency response capacity, and legal accountability in the West Bank in response to the sharp rise in violent settler attacks, intimidation, property destruction, and forced displacement targeting Palestinian communities. The Palestinian Civil Defence (PCD), already operating under severe constraints and growing operational pressures, faces increasing demands for rapid response to attacks while suffering from limited mobility, resources, and infrastructure. Parallel to this, Palestinian civil society organisations (CSOs) play a vital role in documenting violations, supporting victims, and pursuing legal accountability, yet face major challenges linked to access, security risks, and gaps in evidence-collection systems.</narrative>
  </description>
